WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.469
-You know, our next guest
from shows like

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.970
"The Big Bang Theory"
and "True Blood."

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.005
She stars in "Night Court,"
which airs Tuesday nights

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.141
at 8:00, right here on NBC.
Let's take a look.

00:00:08.207 --> 00:00:10.743
-I know that what I did
wasn't technically "legal,"

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:13.779
but I was pushing boundaries
like I do with you.

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.414
It's why we're friends,
and you love that

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:17.683
about me.
-I don't love that about you!

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.652
I don't even like you!

00:00:21.888 --> 00:00:25.425
-But I'm Baby Heather!

00:00:25.491 --> 00:00:29.161
-Your Honor, in light
of this contentious discourse,

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:33.266
I'm wondering if maybe you would
consider recusing yourself?

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.167
-Oh, you think?!

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:38.337
-Please welcome back to the show
Melissa Rauch, everybody!

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:41.740
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:45.478
[ Mid-tempo music plays ]

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:54.821
♪♪

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:56.256
Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.891
-How are you?
-I'm good.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.358
How are you?
-I'm lovely.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:02.295
I'm so happy to have you here,
back in the East Coast.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.530
-I'm back on the East Coast.
-Grew up in New Jersey.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.199
-Jersey, Jersey.
-Yeah!

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.634
-Jersey in the house!
-I hate when that happens.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:11.070
It's always the very back row.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:12.972
-That's where Jersey sits.
Those are my people.

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:14.373
-[ Laughter ] Exactly.
-Hi.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.808
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:18.377
-That's my family.
-Now, you -- We have children

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.946
of similar ages,
and I'm wondering,

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:22.849
do you -- are you seeing
any of your own insecurities

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:24.817
in your kids
as they get a little bit older?

00:01:24.883 --> 00:01:27.554
-It's interesting.
I do feel like being a parent

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.956
just brings up any
unresolved issues that you have.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:34.360
And I'm realizing that I have
some majorly unresolved,

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:37.964
like, latent bullying issues
that I never got over.

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.566
Like we were recently
at a kid's birthday party

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:42.535
at, like, a "paint
your own pottery" place.

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:44.570
And this kid came up to me
and he was like,

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:46.106
"We were all talking.
We want to know,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:49.475
are you an adult or a kid?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.679
And I -- I felt so triggered,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:57.517
and I genuinely wanted to know
who he meant by "we."

00:01:57.583 --> 00:02:00.185
And it came out as,
"Oh yeah?

00:02:00.252 --> 00:02:02.688
Who wants to know?
Who's the "we"?"

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.123
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.189 --> 00:02:06.559
And my husband was like,
"That's a little aggressive.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.862
That's a preschooler."
And so -- Ad I was like,

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:11.531
"Okay, I'm gonna reset."
And I said, "You know,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:14.167
people come in
all shapes and sizes.

00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.035
And I happen to be
on the smaller side."

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.538
He's like, "Oh, no,
we all know you're short.

00:02:18.605 --> 00:02:20.706
We've seen you. It's just
you're covered in paint."

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.674
Alright
.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:24.277
-So it was about
being bad at painting.

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:26.445
-It was about being, like --
and just dripping myself

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.514
in paint like a toddler.
Yeah.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.349
-By the way, nothing says
you're from New Jersey

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.917
more than,
"Oh, who's the 'we'?"

00:02:31.984 --> 00:02:33.285
-Exactly.
-Yeah.

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:35.020
-"Come on, you tell me."
-"Who's this 'we'?"

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:37.957
-I like that you also wanted
to roll up the whole group.

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:39.726
You're like, "I can't just
cut off the head of this thing."

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.093
-Oh, no.
-I got to figure out

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:42.227
who these are.
-Exactly, it's gonna pop up.

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:43.496
-Exactly.
You're gonna use him

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.197
against -- to testify
against the others?

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.566
-Exactly.
-What's it like now

00:02:47.633 --> 00:02:49.768
when you go back home?
You still have family here

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.270
when you visit new Jersey.
Is it nice?

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:53.072
-It's so nice.
It's very nice being back home.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:55.875
We do a lot of, like,
looking through old home videos

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:58.177
and showing them to my kids.
My mom actually pulled out

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.614
an old home video of a community
theater production of "Annie."

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.684
A very Jersey "Annie."
-Now, you were Annie.

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:07.486
-I was Annie.
-How old is this Annie here?

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:11.791
[ Audience awws ]
-I'm about 13.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.626
-Alright.
And so what's a Jersey "Annie"?

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:16.628
-It's a lot of
♪ Ta-morrow, ta-morrow ♪

00:03:16.695 --> 00:03:18.497
♪ I love ya ta-morrow ♪

00:03:18.564 --> 00:03:21.033
That's Sandy.
It's my dawg, Sandy.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.235
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.302 --> 00:03:24.570
-No, I have to say, like,

00:03:24.636 --> 00:03:26.739
I kind of only want to see
New Jersey "Annie" now.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:28.341
-It's pretty great.
It's pretty great.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.810
I might revive it.
Jersey, you ready?

00:03:30.876 --> 00:03:32.811
-Yeah. There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:35.581
[ Both laugh ]
Alright, so, another thing is,

00:03:35.647 --> 00:03:36.815
which I'm very delighted by,

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:40.053
your mother has been
trolling you.

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.954
Now, first of all,
I'm very impressed

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:44.390
because she's trolling you
with a meme,

00:03:44.456 --> 00:03:47.293
which is so beyond
the comprehension of my mother.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.961
Like, I don't even think
she'd know

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:51.230
what any of those words mean.
-That's what's so --

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.598
It's completely shocking,

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.933
because it's very much
not like my mother.

00:03:53.999 --> 00:03:55.434
So someone must
have showed her.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:58.637
Maybe those kids from the
pottery party have gotten her.

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:02.040
But she sends me
these pictures

00:04:02.107 --> 00:04:03.476
whenever I'm on the phone
with her

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.144
or saying anything
that I'm saying with confidence,

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:07.379
that I'm maybe not
100% correct with.

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:10.849
She sends me this meme from me
on "Celebrity Jeopardy!,"

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:13.052
where I was not sure
of my answer.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:14.954 line:0%
-And so you said this
on "Celebrity Jeopardy!"

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:17.456 line:0%
-I did.
-"Yes, I'm sure about it."

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.191
Now, this was an actual moment
that became a meme

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.961
because everybody watching
knew you weren't sure.

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:24.063
-Exactly.
And I knew I wasn't sure.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.498
-Okay, gotcha.
Do you remember

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:26.933
what the question was
that you were not sure about?

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:29.268
-I don't remember,
I think I completely blacked out

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.236
on that entire experience.
-Yeah.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:33.806
-Anything that -- Just
the idea of being questioned --

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:35.708
it didn't matter
what the question was --

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:38.144
it was so much pressure.
-I will say,

00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:40.146
we're both performers,
we've been in front

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:41.580
of an audience.
That strikes me

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.716
as the most stressful thing
you could possibly do.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.517
-It was.
And it's also for charity,

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:48.087
so you really want to do well.
And any question they ask,

00:04:48.154 --> 00:04:50.589
I'm [Laughing nervously].
It's terrifying.

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:52.091
-Did your charity reach
out afterwards

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.526
and say, like, "Thanks, uh,
for nothin'"?

00:04:54.593 --> 00:04:55.861
-Nothin'.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.129
Luckily, it's a charity
that I started,

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:58.764
so I was letting myself down.
-Oh, gotcha.

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.633
So it was a racket.
-Oh! [ Laughs ]

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.301
-Yeah.
So let me -- Just to clarify,

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.337
you started a charity
for yourself...

00:05:04.404 --> 00:05:06.472
-Two win "Celebrity Jeopardy!"
-...and then raised money for it

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:08.474
on "Jeopardy!"
Okay, great.

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.075
Congratulations.
-I'm from Jersey!

00:05:10.142 --> 00:05:12.577
What do you want?!
-"Hey, I'm from Jersey!"

00:05:12.644 --> 00:05:14.780
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:17.449
I mean, really, that would be --
It would be so funny

00:05:17.516 --> 00:05:18.518
if there had been
a "Sopranos" episode

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:20.085
where Tony starts
his own charity

00:05:20.152 --> 00:05:22.421
and goes on "Jeopardy!"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.488 --> 00:05:24.157
-[ As Tony Soprano ]
It's for a good cause.

00:05:24.223 --> 00:05:25.691
-[ As Tony Soprano ]
"Yeah, give me a break!"

00:05:25.758 --> 00:05:28.428
[ Normal voice ] So, your
cos-tar, who was in the clip,

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:30.596
the great John Larroquette,
a giant in comedy,

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:33.265
also a physical giant.
-He is, he is.

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.768 align:end size:91% position:91%
-I could not believe it.
I think he's 6'4".

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.903
-He's 6'4".
-He towers over me,

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.039
and I tower over you.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.106 --> 00:05:43.742
So, what is it like on set
with the great John Larroquette?

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:46.545
-It's -- It's the best,
but it's I also feel

00:05:46.612 --> 00:05:49.682
there's a major imbalance
in our relationship,

00:05:49.748 --> 00:05:52.352
because I, like you said,
I get to work

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.388
with the amazing
comedic force that is John.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:58.824
He is brilliant in every way.
He's 6'4".

00:05:58.891 --> 00:06:02.694
He's got this voice that is like
this hot brick of butter.

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:06.165
Like, he's just - He's amazing.
And he saunters onto set

00:06:06.231 --> 00:06:08.233
and everyone -- just your eyes
go to him

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.304
because he's this incredible,
powerful human being.

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.040
And I also think about John,
you know that song

00:06:15.107 --> 00:06:16.542
"Where Have
All the Cowboys Gone?"

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:18.511
-Yeah.
-I believe

00:06:18.577 --> 00:06:19.879
that they have gone
in to John Larroquette.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:22.014
-He holds
all the old cowboys?

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:23.615
-Yeah.
He's just a cowboy.

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:25.951
He's so -- He's just
a powerful presence.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:28.254
Me, on the other hand,
I hang on him

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:30.589
like I am an Elf on the Shelf.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.691
And I'm so excited
to see him every day,

00:06:32.758 --> 00:06:34.226
that I get to work
with this man,

00:06:34.293 --> 00:06:37.229
that I greet him like an excited
cocker spaniel every day.

00:06:37.296 --> 00:06:38.530
"John, how you doing?
How was your weekend?

00:06:38.597 --> 00:06:39.998
Wanna have lunch?
Wanna talk? "

00:06:40.065 --> 00:06:42.702
And he's so kind
and so wonderful with me

00:06:42.769 --> 00:06:44.703
and, like, just graciously
accepts me

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.238
hanging on him and my hugs.

00:06:46.305 --> 00:06:48.107
But our wonderful writers
on the show

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:50.776
came up with a line
for the season premiere,

00:06:50.843 --> 00:06:52.211
where he says to my character,

00:06:52.277 --> 00:06:53.979
"You're like a puppet
I wouldn't want to buy."

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.749
And, like, it just encapsulates
our entire relationship.

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.484
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.619
-You have wonderful
guest stars on the show.

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:03.489
Um, that was Jessica St. Clair?
-Yes, one of my best friends

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:06.025
in real life.
-And she's just a delight.

00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:09.762
And then one of your
"Big Bang Theory" co-stars here.

00:07:09.828 --> 00:07:13.732
And so just tell me
when someone like Kunal

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:16.601
comes on the show, like,
in front of a live audience,

00:07:16.668 --> 00:07:19.338
it just must be such a delight,
like the "Big Bang Theory" days.

00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:21.640
I mean, people must go nuts.
-It was a dream.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.509
When he came out,
the audience didn't know

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:25.377
that he was going to be
appearing in that episode,

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:26.879
and they went absolutely wild.

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:29.015
And I was just so filled
with delight that he was there.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.050
And we had the best time
all week.

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:32.484
It was just like old times.

00:07:32.551 --> 00:07:34.720
Even that picture actually
was a moment after --

00:07:34.787 --> 00:07:38.624
Kunal is one --
He is just pure heart.

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.927
He's one of the most spiritually
enlightened people I know

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:43.695
and just the most down-to-earth,
wonderful human.

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:45.797
He's also one of the most

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:48.166
impeccably dressed humans
that I've ever met.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.501
-That's a very --
It's a real nice coat.

00:07:49.568 --> 00:07:50.702
-Yes, it's a beautiful coat.

00:07:50.769 --> 00:07:52.838
And he, for years,
has given me a hard time

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.907
about how I roll into work.
For years

00:07:55.974 --> 00:07:57.576
on "Big Bang Theory,"
he showed up to set here --

00:07:57.643 --> 00:07:59.111
and I'm a producer
on the show, too --

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:05.017
and he's like, "Melissa. Still.
You're a producer now.

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:08.020
You're people's boss.
Please put on something nice!"

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:10.556
And Lacretta,
who plays our wonderful bailiff,

00:08:10.622 --> 00:08:12.391
she was like, "Well, you guys
aren't dressed too differently.

00:08:12.458 --> 00:08:13.692
You're both wearing black.

00:08:13.759 --> 00:08:15.494
He's like,
"What are you talking about?

00:08:15.561 --> 00:08:16.995
Like, this is nuts!

00:08:17.062 --> 00:08:20.366
I am in designer clothing,
and she's in Forever 21!

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:23.402
This is not okay!"
And so that picture was taken

00:08:23.468 --> 00:08:26.338
after he gave me a hard time
for my sweatpants.

00:08:26.405 --> 00:08:28.641
-He's a little upset about it.
-He's so angry at me.

00:08:28.707 --> 00:08:30.676
-What a delight
to have you back.

00:08:30.742 --> 00:08:31.777
-Thank you.
-Congratulations

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:33.211
on the continued success
of the show.

00:08:33.278 --> 00:08:34.580
-Thank you so much. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:34.646 --> 00:08:36.915
-Guys, this is
our friend Melissa Rauch.

00:08:36.982 --> 00:08:39.518
"Night Court" is Tuesday nights
at 8:00, here on NBC.

00:08:39.585 --> 00:08:41.120
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

